(Northstar Appliances - March 2026 Incident Review) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Scenario) Tj
T*
(Northstar Appliances runs connected refrigeration systems for grocery and healthcare customers.) Tj
T*
(In March 2026, the team investigated compressor shutdowns after an NS-900 firmware rollout.) Tj
T*
(The same customer accounts appear in the image, audio memo, CSV tickets, and this PDF review.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Key Entities) Tj
T*
(Lakeside Clinic, account C-104, site SEA-17, operated vaccine freezer A.) Tj
T*
(Harbor Market, account C-118, site PDX-04, operated aisle freezer 3.) Tj
T*
(Pine Ridge Foods, account C-122, site BOI-02, operated controller 7.) Tj
T*
(Firmware under review was NS-900 version 4.8.2.) Tj
T*
(Replacement firmware approved for rollout was NS-900 version 4.8.3.) Tj
T*
(Priya Shah owned the field runbook update.) Tj
T*
(Marco Diaz owned the firmware rollout.) Tj
T*
(Elena Brooks owned customer communication.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Timeline And Root Cause) Tj
T*
(On 2026-03-04 at 02:14 local time, Lakeside Clinic opened ticket INC-1043.) Tj
T*
(Vaccine freezer A entered safe mode after three compressor restart attempts.) Tj
T*
(The case was severity P1 because temperature-sensitive medical inventory was at risk.) Tj
T*
(Logs showed firmware 4.8.2 retried the condenser fan check too aggressively after a transient sensor fault.) Tj
T*
(The retry storm increased controller CPU load, delayed telemetry, and triggered safe mode for 47 minutes.) Tj
T*
(The immediate workaround was cold_chain_safe plus a condenser fan service restart.) Tj
T*
(CSV metrics for INC-1043 were severity P1, 184000 dollars of inventory at risk, and 47 downtime minutes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Review Board Decisions) Tj
T*
(The board decided not to roll back every customer to firmware 4.7.9.) Tj
T*
(Rollback would disable telemetry compression required by service analytics.) Tj
T*
(Instead, firmware 4.8.3 rolls out first to healthcare cold-chain accounts, then grocery accounts.) Tj
T*
(Lakeside Clinic qualifies for an SLA credit and a compliance incident summary.) Tj
T*
(Harbor Market receives a preventive maintenance notice, but no SLA credit, because cooling stayed in range.) Tj
T*
(Pine Ridge Foods stays in the pilot group because its delayed defrost was a local night schedule error.) Tj
T*
ET
